    "structuredData": [
      "{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Recipe\",\"name\":\"Buttery Sourdough Buns\",\"description\":\"Soft dinner rolls with a pleasingly mild sourdough tang, buttery spirals that are soft on the inside with a wonderfully crisp crust.\",\"image\":[\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\"],\"recipeIngredient\":[\"3 cups all-purpose flour\",\"0.50 cup sourdough starter\",\"3 cups all-purpose flour\",\"2.50 tsp instant yeast\",\"1 tbsp granulated sugar\",\"1.25 tsp table salt\",\"1 large egg\",\"5 tbsp butter\",\"0.67 cup water\",\"2 tbsp melted butter\",\"0.25 tsp paprika\",\"2 tbsp melted butter\"],\"recipeInstructions\":[{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 1\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/buttery-sourdough-buns#step-1\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Weigh your  3 cups all-purpose flour ; or measure it by gently spooning it into a cup, then sweeping off any excess. Combine all of the dough ingredients,  0.50 cup sourdough starter ,  3 cups all-purpose flour ,  2.50 tsp instant yeast ,  1 tbsp granulated sugar ,  1.25 tsp table salt ,  1 large egg ,  5 tbsp butter , and  0.67 cup water , in a large bowl. Mix and knead, using your hands, a  stand-mixer , or a  bread-machine  set on the dough cycle, to make a soft, smooth dough.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 2\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/buttery-sourdough-buns#step-2\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Place the dough in a lightly greased container, an 8-cup measure works well here, and allow the dough to rise for  1.5-2 hours , until it&apos;s just about doubled in bulk.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 3\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/buttery-sourdough-buns#step-3\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Gently deflate the dough, and transfer it to a lightly greased work surface.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 4\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/buttery-sourdough-buns#step-4\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Roll and pat the dough into a rough rectangle approximately  12 &quot;  x 16&quot;. Put  2 tbsp melted butter  in a small bowl, and add the  0.25 tsp paprika ; it&apos;s there for color, and accentuates the buns&apos; swirl, but omit it if you wish. Spread the dough with the melted butter.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 5\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/buttery-sourdough-buns#step-5\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Starting with a long side, roll the dough into a log.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 6\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/buttery-sourdough-buns#step-6\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Cut the log in  1 &quot;  slices, using a  sharp-knife , or a piece of dental floss looped between your fingers.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 7\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/buttery-sourdough-buns#step-7\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Lightly grease two  8 &quot;  or  9 &quot;  round  cake-pans . Arrange 8 buns in each pan.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 8\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/buttery-sourdough-buns#step-8\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Cover the pans, and let the buns rise for  60 minutes , until they&apos;re noticeably puffy. Don&apos;t let these buns rise too long; you want them to have enough rising power left to expand nicely in the oven. Towards the end of the rising time, preheat the  oven  to 350°F.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 9\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/buttery-sourdough-buns#step-9\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Uncover the pans, and brush each bun with some of the remaining  2 tbsp melted butter .\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 10\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/buttery-sourdough-buns#step-10\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Bake the buns for  22-25 minutes ; they&apos;ll color only slightly.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 11\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/buttery-sourdough-buns#step-11\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Remove the buns from the oven, and turn them out of the pan onto a  cooling-rack . Brush with any remaining melted butter. Serve hot or warm. To reheat, place the buns on a  baking-sheet , tent lightly with aluminum foil, and bake for  10 minutes  in a preheated  350 °F  oven.\"}],\"recipeCuisine\":[\"American\"],\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Brian Sunter\"},\"keywords\":\"sourdough, bread, buns, dinner rolls, baking\",\"recipeYield\":\"16\",\"recipeCategory\":\"bread\",\"tool\":[{\"@type\":\"HowToTool\",\"name\":\"stand-mixer\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToTool\",\"name\":\"bread-machine\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToTool\",\"name\":\"sharp-knife\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToTool\",\"name\":\"cake-pans\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToTool\",\"name\":\"oven\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToTool\",\"name\":\"cooling-rack\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToTool\",\"name\":\"baking-sheet\"}],\"prepTime\":\"PT20M\",\"cookTime\":\"PT3H2M\",\"totalTime\":\"PT3H42M\",\"aggregateRating\":{\"@type\":\"AggregateRating\",\"ratingValue\":\"4.5\",\"ratingCount\":\"1\",\"bestRating\":\"5\",\"worstRating\":\"1\"}}"
    ]
