    "structuredData": [
      "{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Recipe\",\"name\":\"Calzone\",\"description\":\"Traditional Italian stuffed bread, rolled jelly-roll style with your choice of sauce, meats, cheeses, and vegetables.\",\"image\":[\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\"],\"recipeIngredient\":[\"6 cups flour\",\"2 cups lukewarm water\",\"1 tbsp granulated sugar\",\"2.25 tsp instant yeast\",\"6 cups flour\",\"1 tbsp table salt\",\"1 large egg\",\"1 tbsp water\",\"to taste sesame seeds\",\"to taste poppy seeds\",\"3-4 cups water\"],\"recipeInstructions\":[{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 1\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-1\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Weigh your  6 cups flour ; or measure it by gently spooning it into a cup, then sweeping off any excess. Mix  2 cups lukewarm water ,  1 tbsp granulated sugar ,  2.25 tsp instant yeast ,  6 cups flour , and  1 tbsp table salt  together until the dough pulls away from the sides of the bowl. Turn the dough out onto a floured surface to knead.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 2\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-2\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Knead the dough until it is smooth and supple, adding more water or flour as needed.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 3\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-3\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Place the dough in a  mixing bowl . Cover the bowl and allow the dough to rise for  1 hour , or until it is puffy.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 4\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-4\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Gently press the dough down, and turn it out onto a lightly floured surface. Alternatively, you can leave dough in the bowl and let it rise again, for about half the time of the initial rising; this will produce a finer-grained product.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 5\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-5\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Cut your dough into 2 pieces. Roll out each piece into a  10 &quot;  x  14 &quot;  rectangle. Spread a thin layer of sauce on first. Then layer it with your choice of ingredients: sauce (marinara, pizza, pesto, etc.), meat (sliced ham, pepperoni, prosciutto, salami, smoked turkey, cooked and crumbled hamburger, sausage, etc.), cheese sliced or grated (provolone, mozzarella, Parmesan, Gorgonzola, feta, etc.), and vegetables chopped or sauteed (onions, scallions, hot or sweet peppers, mushrooms, garlic, shallots, olives, capers, sun-dried tomatoes, artichoke hearts, spinach, etc.).\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 6\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-6\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Starting with the long edge, roll the dough around the filling jelly-roll style. Pinch the seam and ends together very tightly and place the roll on a  baking sheet  lined with parchment paper.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 7\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-7\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Cover the calzone with a damp towel or plastic wrap (grease the underside of it so it won&apos;t stick to the dough). Let it rise for  45 minutes  to  1 hour .\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 8\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-8\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Preheat your  oven  to 450F. To make the crust crunchy, preheat a  roasting pan  on the oven bottom.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 9\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-9\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Whisk together  1 large egg  and  1 tbsp water  to make a thin glaze.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 10\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-10\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Slash the tops of the loaves, then brush with the egg wash and sprinkle with  to taste sesame seeds  or  to taste poppy seeds , optional. Just before you put the calzone in the oven, pour  3-4 cups water  into the roasting pan.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 11\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-11\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Bake for  15 minutes  at 450F. Turn the heat down to  400 F  and continue baking for a further  15 minutes , or until the crust is golden brown.\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToStep\",\"name\":\"Step 12\",\"url\":\"https://briansunter.com/recipes/calzone#step-12\",\"image\":\"https://briansunter.com/kitchen.jpg\",\"text\":\"Allow the calzone to cool and set for  10-15 minutes . Then cut it in slices.\"}],\"recipeCuisine\":[\"Italian\"],\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Brian Sunter\"},\"keywords\":\"calzone, italian, bread, pizza, baking, main\",\"recipeYield\":\"2\",\"recipeCategory\":\"bread\",\"tool\":[{\"@type\":\"HowToTool\",\"name\":\"mixing bowl\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToTool\",\"name\":\"baking sheet\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToTool\",\"name\":\"oven\"},{\"@type\":\"HowToTool\",\"name\":\"roasting pan\"}],\"prepTime\":\"PT30M\",\"cookTime\":\"PT30M\",\"totalTime\":\"PT3H25M\",\"aggregateRating\":{\"@type\":\"AggregateRating\",\"ratingValue\":\"4.5\",\"ratingCount\":\"1\",\"bestRating\":\"5\",\"worstRating\":\"1\"}}"
    ]
